  "asset_audit_2026_08_04": "Tile and Pure image slugs replaced from the Multipanel asset handoff, then every file was fetched and looked at. Ten of the fourteen are room photography rather than isolated swatches, and one (crystal-marble-large) carries a NEW marketing roundel - so swatch_asset is true for only three. That flag is what stops the hero compositor tiling an image across a shower wall, so it is set from what the file actually shows, not from the filename or the handoff summary. Every URL returns HTTP 200 with distinct bytes; the previous data had Tile and Pure pointing at the same files as each other, which these fix regardless.",
  "asset_audit_2026_08_21": "SUPERSEDES the 2026-08-04 audit for display purposes. Every decor now serves a LOCAL image under /decor-swatches, generated from Grant Westfield's print masters by scripts/build-decor-swatches.mjs; the CDN fields are kept only as provenance and nothing renders from them any more. The masters are full-panel scans at 1:4.138 - the exact 22.75 x 94.5 panel ratio - so unlike the CDN room photography they are genuine flat material captures, which is why swatch_asset is now true for all 21 and the hero compositor can tile any decor. Two caveats, both flagged per-panel: seven masters were CMYK with no embedded ICC profile (color_unverified), and two of those are flat colour chips with no material texture whatsoever (flat_chip). The tile collection was split into large-tile and metro-tile so family matches the price sheet; ids, sku_refs and the 21-decor lineup are unchanged, and the three Grained* display names dropped the prefix since SHIPLAP / WOOD SLAT is the real format differentiator.",
  "pricing_note_2026_08_21": "Prices are per PANEL at 2'x8' nominal (22.75\" x 94.5\" actual), from Nature Panel's Dealer Pricing Structure. That sheet is a framework - format x customer-tier multipliers off landed cost - not a per-SKU list, so the three figures here are the resolved tiers Kitify trades at: cost is the Wholesaler tier (0.41) Kitify buys at, dealer_price is the Dealer 3 tier (0.55) Kitify sells to partners at, and retail_price is MAP. MAP is a GUIDELINE for Kitify's own retail pricing and is NOT enforced on partners - a partner may price above, at or below it. `cost` is Kitify-internal and must never reach a partner- or customer-facing surface. Nature Panel also sells Pure in 4x8 at a different price; Kitify does not stock that format."
}
